kosha calcite

  -- CaCO3. calcium carbonate. the mineral of shells, limestone, marble, chalk.
  -- crystal form: calcite (rhombohedral) or aragonite (orthorhombic) — same formula.
  -- limestone: sedimentary rock, mostly calcite from marine organisms.
  -- marble: metamorphic limestone — recrystallised under heat and pressure.
  -- chalk: soft, fine-grained calcite from microscopic marine algae (coccoliths).
  -- reacts with acid: CaCO3 + 2HCl → CaCl2 + H2O + CO2 (effervesces).
  -- soluble in slightly acidic water (acid rain dissolves limestone buildings).
  -- cement: CaCO3 → CaO (lime) + CO2 at 900°C (calcination).

